KZ3 patch 2058 (RSX pass 57): no draw is skipped while its PSO builds; keycap uploads change only prompt-cell texels.
Menu text corruption (main/campaign menu lists blank, capital C missing; stray glyphs
in "For less"): patch 2048 skipped every draw whose PSO was still building. KZ3 renders its text once per glyph
(stencil-then-cover) into the glyph cache at 0x3A00000 and samples it from there, so a glyph whose draws were
skipped stayed blank, or kept the glyph that held the slot before. The keycap atlas (0x042A9180, the menu prompt
atlas, not a font) was a coincidence: KZ3_KEYCAPS=0 runs on a cold PSO cache lose the same glyphs.
rsx_live_draw.c: a pending PSO entry is waited for (ld_apso_await: the worker wakes the walker through the
condition variable after each finished build); [pso-async] prints awaited= / await= / max= instead of
skipped-draws=. LD_PSO_ASYNC=0 still builds on the walker thread.
rsx_keycaps.h: the caps are drawn into a full-size overlay, then each touched BC3 block is encoded once: freely when
all 16 texels are in cells, else keeping its endpoints and the indices of the texels outside every cell, so those
decode exactly as before (2039 re-encoded shared blocks: 2,030 HUD and 73 menu texels outside the cells changed, up
to 156 / 223 levels, measured on the real atlases). BC3 colour blocks decode in four-colour mode always (2039 used
BC1's c0 <= c1 rule). Host test tools/smoke/test_keycaps.sh case 8 (flips).
